From: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] Pass scalar floating union storage in integer registers on RISC-V

Selecting the largest floating member as the libffi type makes libffi
flatten the union as a floating-point structure. On the RISC-V hardware
floating-point ABI this shifts both the union and subsequent arguments
into the wrong registers. Use an integer of the same size for a union
represented by float or double. Exercise both widths and the neighboring
arguments through the library proxy and direct native calls.

Upstream: pending
Reference: https://github.com/riscv-non-isa/riscv-elf-psabi-doc/blob/9b2767e2a8851709608c4e1452998ad232d6278b/riscv-cc.adoc
Reference: https://github.com/libffi/libffi/blob/v3.8.0/src/riscv/ffi.c
Signed-off-by: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
---
diff --git a/src/com/sun/jna/Structure.java b/src/com/sun/jna/Structure.java
--- a/src/com/sun/jna/Structure.java
+++ b/src/com/sun/jna/Structure.java
@@ -2152,7 +2152,13 @@
                         size = sf.size;
                     }
                 }
-                if ((Platform.isIntel() && Platform.is64Bit() && !Platform.isWindows())
+                if (Platform.isRISCV() && isFloatType(unionType)) {
+                    // The RISC-V psABI passes unions through the integer calling convention,
+                    // including unions whose members are all floating-point scalars.
+                    Pointer storage = unionType.getPointer().equals(FFITypes.ffi_type_float)
+                        ? FFITypes.ffi_type_uint32 : FFITypes.ffi_type_uint64;
+                    unionType = ffiTypeInfo.get(storage);
+                } else if ((Platform.isIntel() && Platform.is64Bit() && !Platform.isWindows())
                     || Platform.isARM() || Platform.isLoongArch()) {
                     // System V x86-64 ABI requires, that in a union aggregate,
                     // that contains Integer and Double members, the parameters
diff --git a/native/testlib.c b/native/testlib.c
--- a/native/testlib.c
+++ b/native/testlib.c
@@ -963,6 +963,14 @@
   return cp;
 }
 
+typedef union { float value; } FloatUnion;
+typedef union { float narrow; double value; } DoubleUnion;
+
+EXPORT double checkFloatingUnions(int first, FloatUnion single, float middle,
+                                 DoubleUnion wide, int last) {
+    return first + 10 * single.value + 100 * middle + 1000 * wide.value + 10000 * last;
+}
+
 typedef union _MixedUnion1 {
   int intValue;
   double doubleValue;
